From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:17:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Safarium: Safari-style tab bar, hover cards, tab
 tear-off, settings cleanup

Work from 2026-11-18 on top of the first checkpoint:

- Settings > Appearance shows only options Safarium honors. Mode now
  drives the native window appearance; "Show home button" adds/removes
  the toolbar Home item (and follows Customize Toolbar); "Customize your
  toolbar" opens AppKit's customization palette. Theme, bookmarks bar,
  tab styling/position, tab search, side panel, split view are hidden.
- Tab capsule matches Safari 26: no nested glass (Tabs toolbar item
  opts out of the Liquid Glass platter), flat gray band, hairline active
  pill, tabs touching (1pt gap), max tab width 24% of the window, equal
  widths while tabs stay >= 260pt.
- Native hover cards (NSPopover): title, origin, page preview, optional
  memory usage; follow the pointer across tabs; correct in full screen.
  Hover card settings re-enabled.
- Tab dragging tracks the whole press itself (reorder works after the
  pressed tab activates). Click edits the address, press-and-move drags
  the tab; arrow cursor unless editing. Dragging a tab out of the bar
  hides it there and shows a page thumbnail; dropping outside the bar
  moves it to a new window, dragging back reinserts it.
- Blank tab: hover close button replaces the magnifier when they would
  overlap.

Local checkpoint only; not intended for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
